@page "/docs/components/vekdatagrid/grouping"
@layout DocumentationLayout

<PageTitle>VekDataGrid Grouping | Vek Components</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-page-layout">
    <article class="docs-article">
        <h1>VekDataGrid: Grouping</h1>
        <p class="docs-intro">Organize products by one or more columns, customize group headers, and collapse groups as needed.</p>

        <section id="live-example" class="docs-section-content" aria-labelledby="live-example-heading">
            <h2 id="live-example-heading">Live example</h2>
            <p>Groups are built from the rows on the current page. A group can appear on more than one page when its rows span pages.</p>
            @if (_products is null)
            {
                <p class="docs-loading" role="status">Loading sample products...</p>
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="docs-example-frame">
                    <VekDataGrid TItem="DemoProduct" Items="_products" PageSize="10" GroupBy="_groups" GroupChanged="OnGroupChanged">
                        <PropertyColumn Property="product => product.Name" Title="Name" Key="Name">
                            <GroupTemplate Context="group">
                                <strong>@group.Title: @group.Value</strong>
                                <span class="group-count">(@group.Count products)</span>
                            </GroupTemplate>
                        </PropertyColumn>
                        <PropertyColumn Property="product => product.Category" Title="Category" Key="Category" />
                        <PropertyColumn Property="product => product.Price" Title="Price" Format="C2" />
                    </VekDataGrid>
                </div>
            }
        </section>

        <section id="code" class="docs-section-content" aria-labelledby="code-heading">
            <h2 id="code-heading">Code</h2>
            <VekCodeViewMulti Tabs="_codeSamples" />
        </section>

        <section id="group-state" class="docs-section-content" aria-labelledby="group-state-heading">
            <h2 id="group-state-heading">Group state</h2>
            <p>Provide an ordered list of <code>VekDataGridGroupDefinition</code> values. Columns can use custom group selectors and group templates. Group headers start expanded; their controls expose <code>aria-expanded</code>, and <code>GroupChanged</code> reports expand/collapse interactions.</p>
            <p>Grouping runs after filtering, sorting, and paging. This keeps paging based on data rows, while a group header can repeat when that group crosses a page boundary.</p>
        </section>
    </article>

    <nav class="docs-toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <h2>On this page</h2>
        <a href="/docs/components/vekdatagrid/grouping#live-example">Live example</a>
        <a href="/docs/components/vekdatagrid/grouping#code">Code</a>
        <a href="/docs/components/vekdatagrid/grouping#group-state">Group state</a>
    </nav>
</div>
